  "summary": "@inetafrica/open-claudia ships Telegram-bot exfiltration and command-execution code",
  "details": "The package bundles multiple scripts (setup.js, health.js, bot.js, core/handlers.js) that combine child_process execution with hardcoded HTTPS calls to api.telegram.org. setup.js and health.js issue https.get/https.request to https://api.telegram.org with POST payloads while reading process.env, process.platform, and filesystem state via fs.existsSync/fs.readdirSync. bot.js spawns child processes and posts data via https to a hardcoded host, and core/handlers.js runs whoami and hostname commands before POSTing results. core/scheduler.js invokes spawn(\"sh\",...) and core/media.js contains multiple POST call sites paired with child_process. The combined shape — reconnaissance commands (whoami, hostname, ping), environment/filesystem reads, and outbound HTTPS to a hardcoded Telegram Bot API endpoint used as a C2/exfil channel — matches operational bot-based exfiltration and remote command handling, not a documented telemetry or agent-inference flow.",
